Sure! Below is a simple example of an **interactive rotating card** using only HTML and CSS.  
When you hover over the card, it rotates 180 degrees around its Y‑axis.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Center the card on the page */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    background:#f0f0f0;
}

/* Card container – perspective gives depth */
.card-wrapper {
    perspective: 1000px;          /* Creates 3D space */
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
    width:300px;
    height:200px;
    position:relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Needed for 3D children */
    transition: transform .6s ease; /* Smooth rotation */
    cursor:pointer;
}

/* Front & back faces */
.card-face {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;     /* Hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius:10px;
    overflow:hidden;
    color:white;
    font-family:sans-serif;
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    font-size:1.5rem;
    text-align:center;
}

.card-front {
    background:#3498db;            /* Front face color */
}

.card-back {
    background:#e74c3c;            /* Back face color */
    transform:rotateY(180deg);     /* Position back face behind front */
}

/* Hover effect – rotate the card */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="card-face card-front">
            <p>Front Side</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="card-face card-back">
            <p>Back Side</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a 3D perspective so the rotation looks realistic. |
| `.card` | Holds both faces and performs the rotation. `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps child elements in 3D space. |
| `.card-face` | Base styling for each face. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the backside when it's turned away from the viewer. |
| `.card-back` | Rotated 180° initially so it sits behind the front face. |
| `.card:hover` | Rotates the whole card 180° on hover. |

Feel free to replace the colors, text, or add images inside the `<p>` tags to suit your design. Enjoy experimenting with this rotating card!
